NVD_LINEAR=1: pitch-linear (DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR) surfaces for nvidia-vaapi-driver v0.0.18.

NVIDIA's Vulkan driver only accepts DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR for NV12 dma-buf imports,
so Chromium's Vulkan video path (the one that avoids X11's DRI3 import) fails
vkCreateImage with VK_ERROR_INVALID_DRM_FORMAT_MODIFIER_PLANE_LAYOUT_EXT on the
driver's block-linear surfaces. With NVD_LINEAR set, surfaces are allocated pitch
linear (RM _FORMAT_PITCH, NVKMS NvKmsSurfaceMemoryLayoutPitch), exported with the
LINEAR modifier in the single-buffer layout, and mapped into CUDA as device memory;
every CUDA copy to or from a surface goes through nvCopySrcPlane/nvCopyDstPlane.
Without NVD_LINEAR the driver behaves exactly as upstream.

